# Cline — coding-agent handover review

`DEVEL.md` is the authority for development, testing, safety and release rules.
Read it before reviewing changes. This file defines only Cline's handover-review
workflow; it must not duplicate or override `DEVEL.md`.

1. Read the owner's request and the other agent's handover. Check the current
   branch, `git status`, the actual diff and relevant source. Preserve existing
   uncommitted work. Verify claimed changes and test results independently.
2. Check for missing requirements, functional regressions, unsafe behaviour and
   unintended changes to the three-tool MCP interface. Review against current
   code and `DEVEL.md`, not against the handover's claims alone.
3. Correct confirmed problems with the smallest change. Follow existing patterns;
   do not add unrelated features, refactor for style, or introduce dependencies
   without owner approval. Do not extend the task beyond the agreed scope.
4. Run applicable offline checks from `DEVEL.md` and focused tests for any
   behaviour changed. Treat live Docker/search checks separately. Never weaken
   a test to make it pass or claim unrun checks passed.
5. Inspect the final diff and update the appropriate user documentation when
   behaviour changes. Report corrections, reasons, checks passed/failed/blocked,
   remaining risks and owner actions. Do not commit, push, merge, tag or release
   unless explicitly authorized.
